To add fields to documents in a MongoDB collection using `mongosh`, you can use the `updateMany` or `updateOne` methods. You can set the `createdDate` and `updatedDate` fields with the current date using the `Date()` function. Here is an example of how to add these fields to all documents in a collection named `myCollection`:

```javascript
use myDatabase;

db.myCollection.updateMany(
    {},
    {
        $set: {
            createdDate: new Date(),
            updatedDate: new Date()
        }
    }
);
```

This command will add the `createdDate` and `updatedDate` fields to all documents in `myCollection`, setting both fields to the current date and time.

If you want to add these fields only to documents that do not already have them, you can use the `$setOnInsert` operator in combination with the `upsert` option:

```javascript
use myDatabase;

db.myCollection.updateMany(
    {
        createdDate: { $exists: false },
        updatedDate: { $exists: false }
    },
    {
        $set: {
            createdDate: new Date(),
            updatedDate: new Date()
        }
    }
);
```

This command will add the `createdDate` and `updatedDate` fields only to documents that do not already have these fields. If the fields already exist in a document, it will not modify them.

